<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 74.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 6-wavelength patch pinned to 2.97e-6 m (3.0 µm, Holocene, 0 Ma). The dispersion sample already correlates with the discrete eigenvalue (Pearson r = 0.999998), and the chronospecies ratios versus Drosophila simulans (27.80) and Drosophila suzukii (33.15) are computed. The Pass 1 path does not sweep Du, does not run the equal-diffusion ablation, and replaces the specimen mask with an all-ones field, so the rendered frame is the activator alone. Huey et al. (2000) measured a latitudinal wing-size cline, not a 3 µm pigment spacing. Overall 74.6/100 (faithfulness 70.4, reproducibility 84.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a89be184699d71a03a1673e1f49d8998944a483a; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 64, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a89be184699d71a03a1673e1f49d8998944a483a, image/png, 876428 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813 (sha256 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813), spec_fingerprint ddf700f45c258daa80240c53b23e60ad30c6cfe8bec1c0e8b9940daf13a758b9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ddf700f45c258daa80240c53b23e60ad30c6cfe8bec1c0e8b9940daf13a758b9; artifact_sha256: 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_subobscura_specimen.jpg=5366640b506b5317..., datasets/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0b9b69eda941b675...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Huey et al. (2000) report that Old World Drosophila subobscura wing length increases with latitude, that North America had no detectable cline one decade after introduction, and that a convergent cline had evolved after two decades. | Turing (1952) shows that a reaction-diffusion system can select a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species reaction; Maini, Painter and Chau (1997) review its use as a Turing system.; reconstructed_in_script: Pass 1 reconstructs k_c for a=0.085, b=1.06, Du=0.041, Dv=0.530 and integrates the nonlinear field from a critical-mode seed (seed 3206).; transfer_boundary: The 3.0 µm wavelength is the assigned subcellular detail scale. It is not a length reported by Huey, Gilchrist, or their coauthors.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Pass 1 activator image is a segmentation of the Cooper 2015 specimen. | Does not claim a parameter sweep or a negative control was executed on the Pass 1 path.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Sweep Du at fixed Dv/Du and show that λ_c increases with sqrt(Du).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add the equal-diffusion ablation and require its maximum growth rate to be negative.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the Cooper 2015 collage and composite the activator into the GIF and the comparison figure.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Report two non-identical specimen estimators (Otsu versus border contrast) plus the KS distance of the growth-rate sample.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.46e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

