<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 1) (Drosophila subobscura)",
        "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Drosophila subobscura morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila subobscura specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila subobscura" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a parameter sweep or a negative control was executed on the Pass 1 path.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the Pass 1 activator image is a segmentation of the Cooper 2015 specimen.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 1 reconstructs k_c for a=0.085, b=1.06, Du=0.041, Dv=0.530 and integrates the nonlinear field from a critical-mode seed (seed 3206).",
        "reported_in_source: Huey et al. (2000) report that Old World Drosophila subobscura wing length increases with latitude, that North America had no detectable cline one decade after introduction, and that a convergent cline had evolved after two decades.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) shows that a reaction-diffusion system can select a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species reaction; Maini, Painter and Chau (1997) review its use as a Turing system.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 3.0 µm wavelength is the assigned subcellular detail scale. It is not a length reported by Huey, Gilchrist, or their coauthors." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila subobscura (Palearctic Latitudinal Wing-Size Cline Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
